# Compatibility Pack

Use when changing a contract consumed by another component, person, or persisted artifact.

- Identify consumers and the before/after behavior of inputs, outputs, errors, formats, and defaults that actually apply.
- Distinguish compatible additions from breaking changes. Preserve accepted behavior or record an explicitly authorized break.
- Consider old/new coexistence and existing stored data when relevant; do not assume a particular protocol or storage engine.
- Verify representative existing consumers and boundary cases using available project checks or scenarios.
- Record migration/recovery limits when a change is irreversible; do not promise rollback without evidence.
